{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>For on this account you withdrew.</b> For since on this account — that the spies frightened you about the Canaanite and the Amalekite who stand there — <b>you withdrew from after HaShem</b>, being afraid to enter the land and not trusting in Him, therefore He will not be with you if you transgress His decree to go to fight, until after forty years. Another interpretation: invert it — 'on this account, that you withdrew.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The abbreviation ד״א resolved as דבר אחר, 'another interpretation.' 'סרסהו' is a rabbinic hermeneutical term meaning to reorder the words of the verse; rendered here as 'invert it.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:01.696374306Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}